TI  - Development and Application of a Questionnaire to Measure Student Attitudes Toward and Understanding of Engineering
PY  - 2017
Y1  - 2017
AB  - This complete research paper will describe the development of a questionnaire that has been applied to measure student attitudes toward and understanding of studies and careers in engineering. The Engineering Attitudes Survey was developed using items adapted from existing instruments, with additional items created to measure course objectives. The questionnaire contains 22 items using a Likert-type format. The survey is being analyzed according to psychometric principles from educational and social psychology research, including item- and instrument-analyses and evaluation of homogeneity/heterogeneity among student responses.
