TI  - Modifying the VALUE Rubrics to Assess the Entrepreneurial Mind-set
PY  - 2019
Y1  - 2019
DO  - 10.18260/1-2--33117
AB  - The engineering entrepreneurship community has focused on assessing the entrepreneurial mindset using the KEEN Framework (curiosity, connections, creating value). This work explores the connection to the VALUE Rubrics developed by the American Association of Colleges and Universities to assess abstract elements such as critical thinking. A full review of the VALUE rubrics has been conducted and the constituent rubric elements reorganized, modified, and repackaged in the form of three new rubrics centered around the KEEN 3Cs. Reliability and validity of the modified rubrics remain to be fully assessed.
